[node name="Label" type="Label" parent="CanvasLayer/TutorialText" unique_id=648621002]
layout_mode = 0
offset_right = 828.0
offset_bottom = 751.0
scale = Vector2(0.815, 0.8093359)
text = "Objective:  
The goal of Scarps is to earn the most points by strategically placing your holodice.

Gameplay:
Placement of Dice:
Players take turns placing holodice on the game board. Dice can be placed in any open space on the board.

Scoring Points:
When a player places dice, they should aim to stack dice with the same number in the same column.
Points are calculated based on the number of identical dice in a column:
If there are two dice with the same number in a column, calculate the score as follows: 
Example: Two 3's = [3 + 3] x 2 = 6 points.
If there are three dice with the same number in a column, the score would be:
Example: Three 3's = [3 + 3 + 3] x 3 = 9 points.
  
Attacking Opponent:
Players can place dice on their opponent's side to \"attack.\"
To do this, there must be an open space available for your die.
Attacking allows you to destroy one of your opponent's dice in a selected column.

Upgrading Dice:
Players can upgrade their dice to enhance their score.
If a die receives a +1 upgrade and is part of a scoring combination:
Example: For the previous example with two 3's, if one of the dice is upgraded, the score will be:
[3 + 3 + 1] x 2 = 7 points.

Winning the Game: 
The game ends when a player has all their columns filled. The player with the highest total score wins. "

